  "instructions": [
    {
      "primary_message": "Wash and dry spinach (skip this step if it came pre-washed). Place spinach and broth in a 6-quart electric pressure cooker insert. Lock lid and set to pressure cook on HIGH for 3 minutes. When done, drape a towel over the vent, manually release the pressure, and carefully open the lid. \n\n",
      "secondary_message": "2 (142 g) pkg baby spinach\n8 cups vegetable broth"
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "When the pressure has been released, change pressure cooker to sauté on HIGH, add tortellini, and stir for a few seconds. Cook, stirring occasionally, until tortellini is just tender, about 5 minutes (or cook according to package instructions). Remove from heat.\n\n",
      "secondary_message": "1 (283 g) pkg cheese tortellini, fresh or frozen"
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Meanwhile, wash, dry, and pick basil leaves off the stems; roll up crosswise and thinly slice into ribbons. Place in a medium bowl, along with eggs, Parmesan, and nutmeg, then whisk to combine.\n\n",
      "secondary_message": "½ small pkg fresh basil\n¼ cup Parmesan cheese, shredded\n¼ tsp nutmeg, ground"
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Slowly pour the egg mixture into the soup, while gently stirring, to separate into ribbons. Add seasoning, then stir once more to combine. \n\n",
      "secondary_message": "1 tsp garlic & herb seasoning"
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "To serve, divide soup between bowls, sprinkle with additional Parmesan, and enjoy!\n\n",
      "secondary_message": "½ cup Parmesan cheese, shredded"
    }
  ],
